{"embedding_dim": 1536, "data": [{"__id__": "chunk-f8d09fcbdc70b03e485805da07644514", "__created_at__": 1756493914, "content": "By default, PF (Personalized feed) will be turned off for all uses browsing in guest mode.", "full_doc_id": "doc-f8d09fcbdc70b03e485805da07644514", "file_path": "unknown_source"}, {"__id__": "chunk-e3b409b80dd09c5f0ebdc50d6251e645", "__created_at__": 1756585546, "content": "{\"feature\": \"Age-specific notification controls with ASL (Age-sensitive logic) (Age-sensitive logic)\", \"feature_description\": \"Notifications will be tailored by age using ASL (Age-sensitive logic) (Age-sensitive logic), allowing us to throttle or suppress push alerts for minors. EchoTrace (Log tracing mode to verify compliance routing) (Log tracing mode to verify compliance routing) will log adjustments, and CDS (Compliance Detection System) (Compliance Detection System) will verify enforcement across rollout waves.\", \"needs_geo_specific_logic\": true, \"reasoning\": \"California law (SB 976 and the California Age-Appropriate Design Code Act) creates state-specific obligations that directly affect this feature. SB 976 (as captured in USCA_SB976.txt) (1) prohibits operators of 'addictive internet-based services or applications' from sending notifications to users who are minors (or whom the operator has not reasonably determined are not minors) during specified time windows unless verifiable parental consent has been obtained; (2) requires operators to provide mechanisms for verified parents to control access; (3) restricts use and retention of age-verification data to compliance purposes and requires deletion immediately after use (except as required by law); and (4) vests enforcement with the California Attorney General and mandates AG rulemaking on age-assurance and parental consent by Jan 1, 2027 (Cal. SB 976, §27006(a)-(c)). The Age-Appropriate Design Code Act (Title 1.81.47, commencing with Section 1798.99.28) requires a DPIA addressing whether design features (including notifications) increase, sustain, or extend childrens' use and forbids uses of a child's personal information that are materially detrimental. Together these provisions require CA-specific implementation: geo-detection ( California-only rules ), local-time and school-day logic, age-assurance/parental-consent flows, DPIA documentation, and auditable but minimized EchoTrace (Log tracing mode to verify compliance routing)/CDS (Compliance Detection System) logs. Material uncertainties remain (e.g., whether our product qualifies as an 'addictive internet-based service or application' under SB 976; the legal meaning of 'reasonably determined' not a minor; and final AG regulations due Jan 1, 2027), so a conservative CA-specific enforcement default (suppress when age unknown) plus readiness to adjust to AG rules is warranted.\", \"regions_affected\": {\"region\": \"California, US (US-CA)\", \"requirement_summary\": \"From Jan 1, 2027, for operators of 'addictive internet-based services or applications' likely to be accessed by children: withhold or throttle notifications to users identified as minors (or where the operator has not reasonably determined the user is not a minor) during restricted windows (12:00 a.m.–6:00 a.m. local time; and 8:00 a.m.–3:00 p.m. local time, Monday–Friday, September through May) unless verifiable parental consent is obtained; provide verified-parent control mechanisms; perform a DPIA per the Age-Appropriate Design Code Act addressing notifications as a design element; restrict and promptly delete age-verification data except as required by law; be prepared for civil enforcement by the California Attorney General and for AG-issued regulations on age assurance and parental consent by Jan 1, 2027.\", \"regulations\": [{\"name\": \"SB 976 – Protecting Our Kids from Social Media Addiction Act (notification/time windows)\", \"citation\": \"USCA_SB976.txt, paragraph (2)\", \"snippet\": \"(2) Commencing January 1, 2027, it shall be unlawful for the operator of an addictive internet-based service or application, between the hours of 12 a.m. and 6 a.m., in the user’s local time zone, and between the hours of 8 a.m. and 3 p.m., from Monday through Friday from September through May in the user’s local time zone, to send notifications to a user whom the operator has not reasonably determined is not a minor, including pursuant to regulations promulgated by the Attorney General, unless the operator has obtained verifiable parental consent to send those notifications.\", \"source_id\": \"USCA_SB976.txt\"}, {\"name\": \"SB 976 – Parental controls / mechanisms\", \"citation\": \"USCA_SB976.txt, paragraph (b)\", \"snippet\": \"The operator of an addictive internet-based service or application shall provide a mechanism through which the verified parent of a user who is a minor may do any of the following:\", \"source_id\": \"USCA_SB976.txt\"}, {\"name\": \"SB 976 – Age-verification data use and deletion\", \"citation\": \"USCA_SB976.txt (age-verification data clause)\", \"snippet\": \"Information collected for the purpose of determining a user’s age or verifying parental consent pursuant to this chapter shall not be used for any purpose other than compliance with this chapter or with another applicable law. The information collected shall be deleted immediately after it is used to determine a user’s age or to verify parental consent, except as necessary to comply with state or federal law.\", \"source_id\": \"USCA_SB976.txt\"}, {\"name\": \"SB 976 – Enforcement and AG rulemaking timeline\", \"citation\": \"Cal. SB 976, §27006(a)-(c) (USCA_SB976.txt)\", \"snippet\": \"27006(a): This chapter may only be enforced in a civil action brought in the name of the people of the State of California by the Attorney General. 27006(b): The Attorney General shall adopt regulations to further the purposes of this chapter, including regulations regarding age assurance and parental consent by January 1, 2027. 27006(c): In promulgating the regulations, the Attorney General shall solicit public comment regarding nondiscrimination", "full_doc_id": "doc-f475a6ff1408c3a8296f4185ed52e177", "file_path": "unknown_source"}, {"__id__": "chunk-10b61ca39028423e6fd0ac51d67bda87", "__created_at__": 1756585546, "content": "(USCA_SB976.txt)\", \"snippet\": \"27006(a): This chapter may only be enforced in a civil action brought in the name of the people of the State of California by the Attorney General. 27006(b): The Attorney General shall adopt regulations to further the purposes of this chapter, including regulations regarding age assurance and parental consent by January 1, 2027. 27006(c): In promulgating the regulations, the Attorney General shall solicit public comment regarding nondiscrimination impacts.\", \"source_id\": \"USCA_SB976.txt\"}, {\"name\": \"California Age-Appropriate Design Code Act (DPIA and child-protection duties)\", \"citation\": \"Title 1.81.47 (commencing with Section 1798.99.28) of Part 4 of Division 3 of the Civil Code (as referenced in USCA_SB976.txt)\", \"snippet\": \"The act requires the business to complete a data protection impact assessment addressing, among other things, whether the design could harm children and whether and how the online product, service, or feature uses system design features to increase, sustain, or extend use of the online product, service, or feature by children, including the automatic playing of media, rewards for time spent, and notifications.\", \"source_id\": \"USCA_SB976.txt\"}]}, \"past_case_references\": [{\"case_id\": \"KG1-PF (Personalized feed)_GuestMode\", \"similarity_reason\": \"Related product behavior: personalization (PF (Personalized feed)) is disabled in Guest Mode — informs design decisions about when personalization/notifications should be suppressed for minors and how to structure product toggles.\", \"source_id\": \"[KG] Guest Mode - PF (Personalized feed)\"}], \"confidence\": 0.85}", "full_doc_id": "doc-f475a6ff1408c3a8296f4185ed52e177", "file_path": "unknown_source"}], "matrix": ""}